    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>British festivals are legendary, chaotic, and completely unpredictable. You start Friday in high spirits with wellies and glitter, and by Sunday afternoon you're dealing with humidity, drizzle, crowded tents, and dry shampoo.</p><p>It is an extreme testing ground for fragrance. Heavy winter gourmands become suffocating in crowded dance tents, while delicate citrus colognes wash away in thirty minutes.</p>"
      }
    },
